ROOT CAUSE

The protected database credential was classified without exposing its value.
It selects an explicit AF_INET PostgreSQL endpoint. The rotation unit allows
only AF_UNIX. systemd therefore blocks the socket family required by the
configured database transport before PostgreSQL can observe the connection.

This is consistent with every R2 exclusion: no PostgreSQL server error, green
runtime-role privileges, green rollback-only lock probe, no publication lease,
no queue/digest conflict and a green isolated PostgreSQL 17 rotation. The
failure is not caused by content, queue state, schema, SQL locking, runtime
role grants, timers, Telegram or any Adult boundary.

MINIMAL REPAIR

Align only the existing rotation unit's address-family allowlist with the
already operating S9 database units: AF_UNIX, AF_INET and AF_INET6. Preserve
all other hardening, the same user, group, working directory, credential,
interpreter, module, arguments and fail-closed controller gates.

DIAGNOSTIC REPAIR

Replace S9_RUNTIME_FAILED-only output with a deterministic bounded taxonomy.
The diagnostic envelope is restricted to stable allowlisted fields and a
fingerprint calculated only from those fields. Exception messages and raw
values remain suppressed. Configuration, contract, database-connect,
database-operation, state, permission, timeout, dependency, CLI and unexpected
failures receive distinct classes and process exit classes.

